      "writtenOn": "2023-03-28T15:32:23Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "While working on adapting this code to the line case (insetting along the \"length\" axis), I realized it was flawed when the base shape had a length less than stroke radius. Currently this renders okay but produces triangles that flip over each other; depth-testing hides this issue. The more problematic case would be when the dimension exactly equaled the stroke radius. Insetting converts the shape to a point and we\u0027d lose all orientation information from the base line/empty rect.\n\nFor this reason I switched to supporting the butt cap outset along only 1 axis in the vertex shader, but it has the nice benefit of consolidating the vertex writing a bit and not having to modify the source geometry at all.",
